course: dictionary
lesson: 12097
title: Coeliac: a word about food and health
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Coeliac is an adjective, so it describes something, like a coeliac diet. It can also be a noun: a coeliac is a person who has coeliac disease. In American English it is often spelled celiac, but the meaning is the same.
explain: Coeliac disease is an illness. When a person with it eats gluten, the gluten damages their gut. Gluten is found in wheat, barley and rye. «Ben has coeliac disease, so he eats gluten-free pasta.» Gluten-free means the food has no gluten in it.
explain: Coeliac disease is not an allergy and not a choice. It is an autoimmune disease, which means the body's own defence system harms the gut. So a coeliac cannot eat ordinary bread, pasta or cake. «Please check the label, because these biscuits might contain gluten.»
fact: Coeliac disease is an illness in which gluten damages the gut.
fact: Gluten is found in wheat, barley and rye.
fact: A coeliac is a person who has coeliac disease.
fact: Coeliac disease is an autoimmune disease, not an allergy and not a choice.
fact: In American English the word is often spelled celiac.
exercise: «Ben has coeliac disease, so he eats gluten-free pasta.» What is coeliac disease? | A sport played at school | A type of cheap bread | *An illness in which gluten damages the gut | A kind of sweet cake
exercise: Which grains contain gluten? | Sugar, salt and water | Milk, cheese and eggs | Apples, carrots and peas | *Wheat, barley and rye
exercise: «Amy is a coeliac, so she must check every label.» In this sentence, what is a coeliac? | A kind of gluten | A teacher at the school | A type of label | *A person who has coeliac disease
test: «Coeliac children cannot eat ordinary bread.» Why not? | *Gluten in the bread would damage their gut | They do not like the taste | Bread is too sweet | Bread is too expensive for them
test: Is coeliac disease an allergy or a choice? | It is a kind of cold | It is a type of allergy to sweets | *It is an autoimmune disease, not a choice | It is a choice, like picking a diet
exam: «At the party, Sam checks the cake label because he is a coeliac.» What is Sam checking for? | Music | *Gluten | Chocolate chips | Candles
